\paragraph{Base model and training.} We fine-tune $\pi_{0.5}$ (openpi) with full parameter updates (not LoRA) on 2$\times$ NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 GPUs (96\,GB each) using PyTorch DDP. Training runs for 30K gradient steps with effective batch size 128, AdamW optimizer with peak learning rate $5 \times 10^{-5}$, linear warmup over 10K steps followed by cosine decay, gradient clipping at max norm 1.0, and bfloat16 mixed precision. The vanilla $\pi_{0.5}$ baseline uses identical architecture, data, and optimization but omits the SDF head and collision-shaping loss, ensuring that any performance difference is attributable solely to the \ours{} training objective. Full hyperparameters are in Appendix~\ref{app:training}.

\paragraph{\ours{} configuration.} The SDF head is a two-layer MLP (263K parameters) attached to the action expert via a forward hook. Loss weights are $\lambda_{\mathrm{SDF}} = 0.1$ and $\lambda_{\mathrm{col}} = 0.01$ with safety margin $\delta = 2$\,cm and noise-aware gating ($t_0 = 0.5$, $\alpha = 10$). Full configuration is in Appendix~\ref{app:geosafe_config}.

\paragraph{SDF ground-truth labels.} Per-timestep signed distance labels are precomputed offline from LIBERO demonstrations using MuJoCo's \texttt{mj\_geomDistance}, covering ${\sim}$75\% of all training tasks (details in Appendix~\ref{app:sdf_labels}).

\paragraph{Benchmarks.} We evaluate on two benchmarks. SafeLIBERO \citep{hu2025aegis} consists of 32 collision scenarios across four suites that mirror the standard LIBERO \citep{liu2023libero} task categories: SafeLIBERO-Spatial (4 tasks), SafeLIBERO-Object (4 tasks), SafeLIBERO-Goal (5 tasks, 4 evaluated per level), and SafeLIBERO-Long (4 tasks with longer horizons). Each suite evaluates 4 tasks at each of two difficulty levels (Level~I and Level~II), yielding 32 collision scenarios in total. We additionally evaluate on standard LIBERO-Spatial (10 tasks) to verify that collision awareness does not degrade manipulation performance on tasks without explicit collision hazards (details in Appendix~\ref{app:safelibero}).

\paragraph{Metrics.} We report three metrics. \emph{Task Success Rate} (TSR): fraction of episodes in which the robot completes the instructed task. \emph{Collision Avoidance Rate} (CAR): fraction of episodes with zero contact with any designated obstacle object. \emph{Safety Score} (SS): $\mathrm{SS} = \mathrm{TSR} \times \mathrm{CAR}$, capturing the joint requirement of task completion and collision avoidance. Each task is evaluated over 50 episodes (seed $= 1$); we report per-suite averages.

